# NCD Code Smell Remediation Plan

**Date:** 2026-05-07  
**Scope:** All source modules (client + service)  
**Audit Method:** 6 parallel explore agents analyzing every `.c`/`.h` file

---

## Mandatory Red-Test-First Policy (Added 2026-05-08)

Project state can be "all tests green" while known defects still exist if tests are skipped or absent. From this point forward, every correctness bug in this plan must be handled with test-first workflow:

1. Add or unskip an exact regression test that fails on current code.
2. Run the relevant harness and capture the failing output.
3. Implement the fix.
4. Re-run and capture passing output.
5. Mark the plan item complete only with red->green evidence.

Rules:
- No P0/P1 correctness item may be fixed without a pre-fix failing test.
- If CI cannot fail immediately, gate known-bug tests with `NCD_ENABLE_KNOWN_BUG_TESTS=1` and run that profile in a required nightly/PR job until fixed.
- Replace SKIP-style known bug tests with fail-when-enabled assertions.
- Every bug item must include: test name, file path, and exact failure condition.

Suggested execution commands:
- `python test/runner.py unit`
- `python test/runner.py integration`
- `python test/generate_report.py`

---

## Bug-to-Test Coverage Matrix (Must Fail Before Fix)

Status legend:
- `MISSING` = no test yet; must add first
- `EXISTS-SKIP` = test exists but does not fail yet; convert to fail-when-enabled
- `EXISTS-RED` = test already fails on baseline

| Plan ID | Status | Test file + test name | Required failing assertion before fix |
|---|---|---|---|
| P0.1 | EXISTS-SKIP | `test/test_service_database.c` -> `TEST(regression_rescan_no_data_loss)` | Service-side rescan replacement must not reduce total dirs to zero; currently should fail when known-bug mode is enabled |
| P0.2 | MISSING | `test/test_service_lifecycle.c` -> `TEST(regression_pending_queue_race)` | Under concurrent enqueue/dequeue, queue invariants (`count`, `head`, `tail`) must remain consistent; current code should show corruption or mismatch |
| P0.3 | MISSING | `test/test_service_lifecycle.c` -> `TEST(regression_service_flags_atomicity)` | Concurrent set/read of control flags must observe ordered transitions; current volatile-only behavior should show missed transitions under stress |
| P0.4 | MISSING | `test/test_shared_state.c` -> `TEST(regression_crc64_init_race)` | Concurrent first-call `shm_crc64()` must produce deterministic checksum and no partial-table corruption |
| P0.5 | MISSING | `test/test_matcher.c` -> `TEST(regression_name_index_concurrent_rebuild)` | Parallel `matcher_find()` on same DB must not crash/UAF and must return stable counts |
| P0.6 | MISSING | `test/test_service_integration.c` -> `TEST(regression_scan_matcher_concurrency)` | Concurrent scan+query must not crash and must keep result paths valid across iterations |
| P0.7 | MISSING | `test/Win/test_platform_win.c` (or new `test/test_platform_ncd.c`) -> `TEST(regression_ncd_con_init_once)` | Parallel first print/init must open console handle once and avoid leaked duplicate init |
| P0.8 | MISSING | `test/test_service_lazy_load.c` -> `TEST(regression_shm_publish_gap)` | Client reads during publish must not observe SHM missing/not-found window |
| P1.1a | MISSING | `test/test_service_integration.c` -> `TEST(regression_version_check_not_found_parity)` | Windows and POSIX must return identical result when service stops during version check |
| P2.20 | MISSING | `test/test_service_database.c` -> `TEST(regression_status_message_pointer_lifetime)` | Returned status message must remain valid after lock boundaries and concurrent updates |

Execution requirement per row:
- Baseline run: demonstrate failure with known-bug mode enabled.
- Post-fix run: same test must pass with known-bug mode still enabled.

