## ðŸŸ  P1 â€” High-Impact Performance & Duplication

### P1.1 â€” Extract shared IPC protocol logic (~300+ duplicated lines)
- **Files:** `src/control_ipc_win.c` + `src/control_ipc_posix.c`
- **Duplicated:** `ipc_error_string()`, `ipc_client_get_state_info()`, `ipc_client_get_detailed_status()`, `ipc_client_get_version()`, `ipc_client_check_version()`, `ipc_server_send_response()`, `ipc_server_send_error()`, `ipc_server_send_version_mismatch()`, 6 thin client API functions
- **Fix:** Create `src/control_ipc_common.c` with all payload-serialization/deserialization and error mapping. Platform files keep only `send_receive()` and connection management.
- **Also fixes P1.1a:** `ipc_client_check_version()` has a behavioral inconsistency â€” Windows treats `NCD_IPC_ERROR_NOT_FOUND` as success after shutdown; POSIX doesn't.

### P1.2 â€” Atomic write pattern duplicated in 5 sites
- **Files:** `src/database.c` â€” `db_save_binary_single` (314â€“344), `db_save_binary` (1419â€“1486), `db_config_save` (474â€“501), `db_set_skipped_rescan_flag` (2055â€“2086), `db_metadata_save` (2703â€“2774)
- **Problem:** Same `.tmp` â†’ `.old` backup â†’ rename â†’ clean pattern repeated with subtle variations.
- **Fix:** Extract `db_atomic_write(path, buf, size, with_backup)` function.

### P1.3 â€” Directory rebuild (remove + filter-excluded + remove-subtree) triplicated
- **File:** `src/database.c` lines 928â€“988, 1164â€“1303, 3457â€“3535
- **Problem:** Three identical blocks: mark descendants, build `old_to_new` map, allocate `new_dirs`/`new_pool`, copy surviving entries, update parents, free old arrays.
- **Fix:** Extract `drive_rebuild_filtered(drv, to_remove_bitmap, rebuild_pool)`.

### P1.4 â€” `metadata_transaction()` pattern repeated ~15 times in main.c
- **File:** `src/main.c` lines ~4951â€“5316
- **Problem:** Every metadata mutation (group add/remove, exclusion add/remove, history clear/remove) independently implements `is_service_backend()` branch:
  ```
  if (service) { send IPC } else { load meta, modify, save, free }
  ```
- **Fix:** Create `static bool with_metadata(MetadataMutator fn, void *ctx)`.

### P1.5 â€” `platform_build_drive_root()` duplicated 5+ times in main.c
- **File:** `src/main.c` lines 1740â€“1756, 1882â€“1890, 5810â€“5812, 810â€“850
- **Problem:** Same Windows/Linux `#if` block for constructing a drive root path.
- **Fix:** Extract into platform helper.

### P1.6 â€” `agent_load_target_db()` duplicated 4 times in main.c agent dispatch
- **File:** `src/main.c` lines 5470â€“5582
- **Problem:** AGENT_SUB_QUERY, AGENT_SUB_TREE, AGENT_SUB_COMPLETE, AGENT_SUB_CHECK each duplicate the same 18-line "check db_override â†’ get CWD â†’ get drive â†’ load DB" block.
- **Fix:** Extract `static NcdDatabase* agent_load_target_db(const NcdOptions *opts)`.

### P1.7 â€” `platform_error_to_result_code()` duplicated 6+ times
- **File:** `src/main.c` lines 3132â€“3149, 3321â€“3342, 3828â€“3845, 4080â€“4091, 4226â€“4246, 4284â€“4317
- **Problem:** Each agent mutation function independently classifies Windows `GetLastError()` / Linux `errno` into result code strings.
- **Fix:** Extract `static const char* platform_error_to_result_code(void)`.

### P1.8 â€” `apply_filter()` O(N) full scan on every keystroke
- **File:** `src/ui.c` lines 1324â€“1346
- **Problem:** Every typed character in the selector filter scans ALL matches to rebuild the `filtered[]` index. With 100K+ results, this is ~6MB of string comparisons per keystroke.
- **Fix:** Build a character-level inverted index or pre-segment results by first-character prefix.

### P1.9 â€” `nav_reload_lists()` O(N) filesystem enumeration on every arrow key
- **File:** `src/ui.c` lines 1585â€“1611
- **Problem:** Every UP/DOWN/LEFT/RIGHT in the navigator calls `con_list_subdirs()` (kernel: `FindFirstFileExA`/`opendir` + `readdir` loop + `qsort`). Browsing a folder with 10K items re-sorts on every key.
- **Fix:** Cache siblings/children per directory node. Only reload when the directory actually changes.

### P1.10 â€” `db_filter_excluded()` O(D Ã— depth Ã— E) per directory
- **File:** `src/database.c` lines 1176â€“1204
- **Problem:** For each directory, calls `db_full_path()` (walks parent chain, O(depth)) then `db_exclusion_check()` (scans all exclusion patterns with `wildcard_match`, O(E)). With 100K dirs, 50 exclusions, avg depth 5 â†’ ~25M operations.
- **Fix:** Pre-compute full paths once. Pre-compile exclusion patterns into a regex/trie. Filter during scan rather than post-hoc.

### P1.11 â€” `db_remove_path()` O(N Ã— depth) linear scan
- **File:** `src/database.c` lines 928â€“936
- **Problem:** Linear scan through all dirs, each calling `db_full_path()` + `_stricmp`. For 100K dirs at depth 5, ~500K string operations per removal.
- **Fix:** Build a full-path â†’ index hash map on database load, or maintain during scan.

### P1.12 â€” `matcher_find()` fallback: full O(N) scan for all prefix searches
- **File:** `src/matcher.c` lines 389â€“418
- **Problem:** The `NameIndex` hash table only works for exact name matches. Every prefix search ("NewCh") falls back to scanning all 200K directories.
- **Fix:** Build the bucket table (already has `bucket_starts`/`bucket_count` fields, never populated). Or use a trie/suffix array.

### P1.13 â€” `matcher_find_fuzzy()` full O(N Ã— V) scan with no pruning
- **File:** `src/matcher.c` lines 743â€“798
- **Problem:** For N=200K directories and V=3 digit variations, 600K `dl_distance()` calls. Each DL is O(mÃ—n) for string lengths â€” up to 16M operations.
- **Fix:** Use n-gram indexing to prune candidates. Pre-compute path lengths. Cache `strlen(s1)` (invariant across loop).

### P1.14 â€” `scan_ctx_is_excluded()` O(D Ã— E) per directory
- **File:** `src/scanner.c` lines 238â€“297
- **Problem:** Every scanned directory entry tests all exclusion patterns with recursive wildcard matching.
- **Fix:** Pre-compile exclusions into a DFSA or regex. Short-circuit on common prefixes.

### P1.15 â€” `agent_json_escape` duplicated, emits character-by-character
- **File:** `src/main.c` lines 1065â€“1084 and 2752â€“2775
- **Problem:** Two implementations: one to stdout via `fputc`, one to buffer. The stdout version emits one `fputc` per character â€” a syscall per byte for non-escaped characters.
- **Fix:** Unify into buffer-based version. Flush after complete JSON object. Use `setvbuf(stdout, NULL, _IOFBF, 65536)`.

### P1.16 â€” PathMap built+destroyed per query (O(D) allocation per op)
- **File:** `src/main.c` lines 1864, 2137, 2405
- **Problem:** `agent_mode_tree`, `agent_mode_check`, and `add_path_to_database` each allocate a fresh PathMap (500K hash entries), fill it, use it for one lookup, then free. For a large database, this is ~4MB allocation per query.
- **Fix:** Cache the PathMap on `NcdDatabase`, invalidate on mutation.

### P1.17 â€” SID acquisition duplicated between IPC and SHM Windows files
- **Files:** `src/control_ipc_win.c` (107â€“132) + `src/shm_platform_win.c` (468â€“498)
- **Problem:** `OpenProcessToken` â†’ `GetTokenInformation` â†’ `ConvertSidToStringSidA` â†’ `LocalFree` sequence duplicated with identical fallback to `WTSGetActiveConsoleSessionId`.
- **Fix:** Extract `get_user_sid_string()` into a shared Windows utility.

### P1.18 â€” 85% duplicated scan loop between Windows and Linux
- **Files:** `src/scanner.c` lines 877â€“1016 (Windows), 1023â€“1156 (Linux)
- **Problem:** Both `platform_scan_directory()` implementations share core stack/frame/push/exclusion-check/progress logic. Only directory enumeration API differs.
- **Fix:** Extract traversal skeleton into `do_scan()` with function pointers for `open_dir`, `read_entry`, `close_dir`.

### P1.19 â€” `db_full_path()` walks parent chain twice (depth count + name collect)
- **File:** `src/database.c` lines 1019â€“1151
- **Problem:** First pass counts depth walking parent chain; second pass re-walks the same chain to collect names. Two full pointer-chase traversals for every path.
- **Fix:** Push names onto a growable stack during first pass, pop during path construction.

### P1.20 â€” `db_set_skipped_rescan_flag()` reads/writes entire 200MB file for 1 byte
- **File:** `src/database.c` lines 2029â€“2072
- **Problem:** `malloc(file_size)` â†’ `fread` entire DB â†’ modify 1 byte â†’ `fwrite` entire DB. For a 200MB database, this is 400MB of I/O.
- **Fix:** `fseek` to `offsetof(BinFileHdr, skipped_rescan)`, `fwrite` 1 byte, `fflush`.

