## DeepSeek Parallel Subagent Execution Blueprint

Objective: remediate all plan items with maximum parallelism while preventing merge conflicts and hidden regressions.

### Coordinator Rules

1. Do not assign overlapping write scopes to two subagents.
2. Every subagent must deliver in this order:
   - add failing tests for owned bug items
   - prove red
   - implement fix/refactor
   - prove green
3. Each subagent must list changed files explicitly in handoff notes.
4. Integrator runs full suite after each wave:
   - `python test/runner.py unit`
   - `python test/runner.py integration`
   - `python test/generate_report.py`

### Parallel Workstreams (Disjoint Ownership)

1. Subagent A - Service rescan and runtime flags
   - Owns: `src/service_main.c`, `test/test_service_database.c`, `test/test_service_lifecycle.c`
   - Items: P0.1, P0.3, P3.7
2. Subagent B - Service queue and state synchronization
   - Owns: `src/service_state.c`, `src/service_state.h`, `test/test_service_lifecycle.c`, `test/test_service_database.c`
   - Items: P0.2, P2.20, P3.6
3. Subagent C - Shared memory publish and snapshot plumbing
   - Owns: `src/service_publish.c`, `src/service_publish.h`, `src/shm_platform_*.c`, `test/test_service_lazy_load.c`, `test/test_shared_state.c`
   - Items: P0.4, P0.8, P2.9, P3.8
4. Subagent D - Matcher concurrency and algorithmic hot paths
   - Owns: `src/matcher.c`, `src/matcher.h`, `test/test_matcher.c`, `test/bench_matcher.c`
   - Items: P0.5, P1.12, P1.13, P2.11, P2.12, P2.17
5. Subagent E - Scanner/database mutation safety and DRY extraction
   - Owns: `src/scanner.c`, `src/database.c`, `src/database.h`, `test/test_database.c`, `test/test_service_integration.c`
   - Items: P0.6, P1.2, P1.3, P1.10, P1.11, P1.14, P1.19, P1.20, P3.1, P3.2, P3.16, P3.17
6. Subagent F - Agent mode/main/CLI dedup and platform boundary cleanup
   - Owns: `src/main.c`, `src/cli.c`, `src/platform_ncd.c`, `src/platform.c`, `test/test_bugs.c`, `test/Win/*`, `test/Wsl/*`
   - Items: P0.7, P1.4, P1.5, P1.6, P1.7, P1.15, P1.16, P2.1, P2.2, P2.3, P2.4, P2.6, P2.15, P3.4, P3.5, P3.10, P3.12, P3.14, P3.15
7. Subagent G - IPC cross-platform consolidation
   - Owns: `src/control_ipc_win.c`, `src/control_ipc_posix.c`, new `src/control_ipc_common.c/.h`, `test/test_service_integration.c`
   - Items: P1.1 (and P1.1a behavior parity regression test)
8. Subagent H - UI performance and DRY consolidation
   - Owns: `src/ui.c`, `src/ui.h`, `test/test_bugs.c` (or new UI-focused tests)
   - Items: P1.8, P1.9, P2.5, P2.7, P2.10, P3.11

### Wave Schedule

1. Wave 1 (all subagents): add failing tests only for owned bug/correctness items.
2. Wave 2 (A/B/C/D/E/F/G): implement P0 fixes in parallel after red proof captured.
3. Wave 3 (D/E/F/G/H): implement P1 high-impact refactors and performance work.
4. Wave 4 (F/H + any free capacity): P2 cleanup/table-driven work.
5. Wave 5: P3 backlog opportunistic improvements.

### Completion Gate for Every Item

- [ ] Failing regression test exists and is reproducible on baseline.
- [ ] Fix merged with owned scope only.
- [ ] Regression test now passes.
- [ ] No new failures in unit/integration/full report.
- [ ] Plan item marked done with links to test evidence.

